Start();
include(utilities);
showPath.path = "/tmp/incantTest.pdf";
viewer = 0;
register(ColorListT);
search ColorListT list;
define
    clSay code={
        csC := registries["cOLOr"];
        csB := *csC["black"];
        csW := *csC["white"];
        csBt = string $*csB$;
        csWt = string $*csW$;
        csD := registries["dESCRIPTIONs"];
        csE := *csD["black"];
        csEt = string $*csE$;
        cerr "CL-4 cOLOr black [" csBt "] white [" csWt "] its description [" csEt "]":;
        };
    clRead path="/tmp/incantTest.pdf";
    ;
show(colorList);
clSay();
readPDF(clRead);
cerr "COLORLISTT SENTINEL":;
stop();

colorListT -- the colours as a poured list, IncantForms/Windows/colorList, shown through the stash (SEQ 741; derived rows since SEQ 742).
Tester's final shape is Start(); show(colorList); -- this is that, with utilities loaded first so showPath can point at
test.pdf and never at Tony's output.pdf. The form holds pour:=cOLOr and no row: pour derives each row (pourDeriveT pins that).
CL-1  the stash finds colorList (a deferred line), and it draws to test.pdf.
CL-2  14 rows: the names in cOLOr's order.
CL-3  the swatches print the values, white on black, blue and darkBrown and black on the other eleven; 14 descriptions.
CL-4  loading the form leaves cOLOr as it was: black is #000000, white #ffffff, and black's description is dESCRIPTIONs' own words.
      (The form defines its descriptions with only Grokking searched. With cOLOr on the list, black="..." reopened cOLOr's
      black and overwrote it: measured 2026-11-22, and the H7 for this row.)
CL-5  the page is as tall as its rows need (height=fit): 40 + 14 x 24 + 13 x 4 + 2 x 12 = 452, read off the PDF.
